{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: archive fixed-parent fix at exact head d51c93566457e7b51b99632ef5479c9783a360f3, tree c7c368b110ef28a73a619588e059ff46830d5f62 (review request 85c61359, promise c6638675, implementation fc2548ae / 28cdea0d). There is one required documentation finding (F1), which planner ruling b01b27bd asks me to raise before approval. I found no code defect, and everything else I checked passes. A successor that changes only the note needs no new gate (docs/testing.md:597) and only a short review.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-archive-fixed-parent.md (artifact f38076f9), first and in full. Then I read the production diff from Main d7aea0b0:\n- Git: http-read.ts, journal-v2-frontier.ts, journal-v2-append.ts, journal-v2-tree.ts, journal-v2-preparation.ts, journal-anchor-legacy.ts, journal-anchor-legacy-count.ts and journal-objects.ts;\n- Scope: archive-driver.ts, archive-frontier-store.ts, archive-frontier-cost.ts, archive-bootstrap-cost.ts, archive-host.ts, archive-parent.ts, archive-adaptive.ts, archive-build.ts and archive-row.ts.\nAfter that I read the migration and parent-state tests and the committed evidence.\n\nF1 (required). Ruling e6e456e4 point 1 says the note gives the measured maximum nodes and metadata per pass, and the margin to 64 nodes and 4 MiB. Ruling b01b27bd says to ask for the margin before approval if it is missing. The note gives maxima but no margins, and for the migration fixtures it gives only the seed costs. From the committed post-gate-repair/measurements.json, the margins are:\n- installed Grow production cohort: maxima 57 nodes, 3,566,747 metadata and 62,328,993 input work, so margins of 7 nodes, 627,557 metadata and 4,779,871 input work. The maxima need not come from one pass.\n- Native300 drain: maxima 47 nodes, 3,465,411 metadata and 38,828,099 input work, so margins of 17 nodes, 728,893 metadata and 28,280,765 input work.\n- 6-pass, 37-pass and padded 37-pass migrations: only the seed passes are measured, at 18 nodes and at most 475,240 metadata, so margins of 46 nodes and at least 3,719,064 metadata. The test asserts that the native passes after migration confirm, but their costs are not recorded.\nRequested fix: state these margins in the note, labelled as measured local fixture values. For the migration fixtures, either give the measured costs of their native passes or say plainly that only the seed passes were measured. Include input work as well, because the Grow cohort uses 93% of it. No code, test or seal change is needed, and no new run unless the planner asks for the migration fixtures' native-pass costs.\n\nContinuation conditions (ruling b01b27bd): all four hold.\n1. From e9511c43 (tree ee29d841) to d51c9356, only two paths outside notes/ differ: packages/git/test/journal-v2-budget.test.ts and packages/scope/test/archive-host.test.ts. From the tested b86df6e5 (tree 397762ef) to this head, 23 paths change, all under notes/.\n2. The committed gate-failure-excerpts.txt shows \"Tests 3 failed | 3517 passed | 3 skipped (3523)\" across 494 files. It equals its source minus one surplus final newline, as its manifest row declares. One Git case received 25 nodes where 31 was expected. The two host cases received attempts 25, nodes 10, calls 50, metadata 22,774 and inputWork 89,628. Each new expected value equals the received value exactly. Every gate stage before the tests exited 0, and Node 37 and Counting 55 were not reached.\n3. At b86df6e5, both whole files passed: 13 cases (1 Git, 12 host), exit 0, no signal. Node 37 (37 of 37) and Counting 55 (55 of 55) passed, both children with exit 0 and no signal. Both independent audits are committed.\n4. The duplicate-ready error came from the builder's outer runner, not from the repository gate. Its uniqueness check runs after the child exits, and it rejected two ready records 10 ms apart for one passing Scope case. It did not cause or hide any test failure, all 3,523 identities reconcile, and the failed gate is not relabelled. The repository gate counts only the child's result, so no further source needs covering.\n\nRequest and rulings.\n- fc2548ae: the 200-append parent-state witness completes with no remote parent read. The native-dispatch control fails at pass 25, at 8,703 \u003e 8,487 tree bytes. No response guard or byte limit widens, and ARCHIVE_BOUNDS is unchanged. The note weighs options (a), (b) and (c) and gives its reason for (b).\n- 63a9216f: migration reads only the confirmed commit, at depth 1 with blob:none, through SmartHttpSource.currentParent. That read has these limits:\n  - the wanted commit is at most 1,024 bytes;\n  - every companion must be a tree;\n  - trees total at most 18 KiB;\n  - at most 660 objects and 32 KiB on the wire.\n  It adds one exact head-blob read of at most 1,024 bytes, as in my reading of the ruling. The migration pass archives no entries and creates no receipt, Mark, attempt or wake. The complete-closure bootstrap is gone: selectArchiveBootstrapBounds is removed, and provider.objects is used only by the existing pending path for the older layout. There is no stopgap fallback. The tests show:\n  - histories of 6, 37 and padded 37 passes (1,754, 9,349 and 16,433 tree bytes; the last is at least 16,384) migrate in one pass and then confirm native passes;\n  - an over-bound tree refuses with neither native key installed;\n  - a wrong commit, incarnation or head hash refuses with the row and keys unchanged;\n  - an old pending Mark confirms by readback, or seeds only its exact confirmed parent and then resends once.\n- e6e456e4: installed Grow passes, with no change to archive-installed.test.ts. Native passes after migration confirm in the 6-pass and 37-pass fixtures. Native300 drains 300 entries in nine prefixes (34, 35, 35, 35, 35, 34, 35, 34 and 23) with no remainder. The fit is cold: it uses the through-bound profile and shared validation, not a warm memo. Only the margin is missing (F1).\n\nDocument checks at d51c9356:\n- git diff --check -B against d7aea0b0 is clean;\n- check-commit-messages reports 31 checked, 0 flagged;\n- section citations, run on an export, report 1,876 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved. The script is identical to Main's.\nEvidence: the evidence folder holds 91 tracked files, all accounted for by three manifests (86 rows, two authored decision files and the three manifests). Every row matches its committed bytes and SHA-256. 85 of the 86 equal their original external file; the one exception is the declared one-byte derivation above.\n\nArchitecture: the driver keeps the existing receipt and Mark protocol. It adds a bounded native witness of 11 objects (the commit, nine path trees and the head blob) to the scope's own SQLite. Private tokens guard that state, with compare-and-set at stage (together with markAttempt) and at promote (together with confirm), each inside one outer transaction. Steady-state appends read parent objects only from this witness. An unpublished old receipt keeps a separate, bounded remote source for old pass manifests. One new transport method serves the one-time migration. The cost of the design is about 12 more nodes per pass than Main on the matched published path, and fewer entries per pass: 34 to 35 in the drain fixture, against 41 to 44 on Main. The note states the remaining fit-risk band (53 to 64 nodes on Main) and claims no general first-entry capacity, which e6e456e4 allows.\nSecurity: I found no defect.\n- Integrity rests on the locally confirmed receipt. The witness binds the format, repository digest, scope and incarnation, commit and through head (the sequence and hash in head.json). The existing reader hash-checks every object.\n- Stored state is decoded under size bounds, and fully revalidated against the current receipt on every load. Forged or corrupt state refuses, with no remote fallback. Only an authenticated contradiction of the current pending Mark stops the journal, with reason rebuild-mismatch.\n- The migration read uses the same repository read credential and one exact want. It admits only the commit and trees, then one blob. Wire bytes, inflation, objects and copies are each charged before the work they pay for. The source cannot be reused after currentParent.\n- Append verification still requires a changed head.json with an increasing through in both scopes. The new headSeen guard refuses a rewrite that does not change the head, and its control matched.\n- No new I/O path, credential, route or authority is added.\nSimplification: the change is large, with 37 files outside notes/ and about 3,000 lines, but each part has one job:\n- the frontier codec and validator in Git;\n- the store and its costs in Scope;\n- one transport method;\n- driver wiring, which replaces the old #copy and #parent with shared helpers.\nTwo leftover names could be tidied later; this is nonblocking. archive-bootstrap-cost.ts now holds only the migration bounds, and the host's oneClosure parameter and its comment still describe a complete pack. The evidence is heavy, but manifests pin it and it has no effect at runtime.\n\nFindings: F1 only, a required documentation change. I found no code finding.\n\nResidual risk, for the planner's deploy:\n- These are local fixture results; nothing has run hosted.\n- Room A's current tree (8,698 bytes, 462f064f) is under the 18 KiB migration bound, so it should migrate in one pass and then run native passes.\n- A journal whose receipt has anchorsPublished false still reads its old pass manifests through the bounded stopgap source on its first native pass. Under Main's code, the first confirmed pass after an unpublished receipt publishes its anchors; the 78638def drain asserted anchorsPublished on every receipt. So the journals that have run since 21:18 on 23 October should already be published, and the three one-commit journals are far below 8,487 tree bytes. This is my reading of the code, not a hosted check.\n- A first entry that needs 53 to 64 nodes on Main can now refuse. After the deploy, the planner's journal reads should watch for refusals with reason limit at the plan step.\nDeployment is planner-owned.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f38076f9a865e802538c73a71913384efc099468","binding":"assigned","head":"d51c93566457e7b51b99632ef5479c9783a360f3","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c663867526a96b632ce6221ec762c4fe52d3f20d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:28cdea0d83a29e9a02c5107d89c6e21b10341fc2\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c663867526a96b632ce6221ec762c4fe52d3f20d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}